WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.280
Send me information.

2
00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:02.800
Start by agreeing.

3
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:03.600
Sure.

4
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.080
What would be most
useful:

5
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.080
how the approval
process works,

6
00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.240
or an example from a
similar company?

7
00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:11.120
Let the buyer choose.

8
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:12.920
Say they want the
example.

9
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.480
Send that one item
with a short note

10
00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.760
about what you
discussed.

11
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.000
Then ask,

12
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:19.960
Would a quick call
Thursday help you

13
00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.240
decide whether it fits?

14
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.860
Only schedule the
follow-up if they

15
00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:24.260
agree.

16
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.460
If they just want the
information,

17
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:27.900
send what you
promised.

18
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.180
Record the request
accurately.

19
00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.250
An information
request is not a

20
00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:32.940
booked meeting.

